/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Our company is driven by a team of professional metallurgists committed to manufacturing the highest quality ferrous metals. Varaha Metaliks Pvt. Ltd boasts a robust annual manufacturing capacity of 7,200 metric tons, facilitated by cutting-edge laboratory and testing facilities that include UTM, BHN, sand testing equipment, metal chemical composition analyzers, and hydro testing among others. Our state-of-the-art manufacturing technology and highly qualified technical team ensure that each product adheres to the stringent BIS & ISO quality standards. VMPL is equipped with both machine moulding featuring 450 and 900 ARPA and hand moulding facilities, capable of casting single pieces weighing up to 1.5 metric tons.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (To deliver superior products that exceed ISO standards through advanced manufacturing and rigorous quality control. We invest in cutting-edge technology and innovative practices to produce reliable ductile iron pipe fittings, manhole covers, and ferrous alloy castings. Our commitment to sustainability minimizes our environmental footprint and benefits the communities we serve. By leveraging our metallurgists' expertise and fostering continuous learning, we maintain our competitive edge and build long-term customer relationships through tailored solutions and exceptional service.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Pvt. Ltd stands as a prominent casting manufacturer in India, specializing in Ductile Iron Pipe Fittings, DI Manhole Covers, and Ferrous Alloy Castings. Guided by the Mittal, Jhunjhunwala and Jaju families, distinguished entrepreneurs with over 4 decades of expertise in the FERROUS METAL, WATER, INFRA and other diverse sectors. With a approx annual production capacity of 7,200 metric tons, also equipped with advanced laboratory and testing facilities. The company is BIS and ISO certified upholding strict quality standards, employing both machine and hand molding techniques.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
